@@ -1,6 +1,15 @@
+
+- Saved highlight handles can extend or shorten across adjacent pages in the same chapter; edge dragging loads the actual page and saves once on release.
+
+- Saved highlights stop at the selected text before a joined dash; the floating Edit/Delete toolbar has larger high-contrast icons. Highlights also continue across page breaks inside hyphenated words, without changing saved clipping text.
+
+- Highlights are grouped under collapsible chapter headers with counts; opening and deleting a highlight preserve its original identity.
+- Touch-drag highlights reuse the existing bounded selection snapshot instead of repainting the page for each word; the drag cursor is fully cleared when the selection moves.
 ## [v1.6.1] - 2026-10-03

 ### Added
+
+- crASHink: tapping a highlight opens a word editor with start/end extension and trimming, a paged text preview with surrounding context and a visibly marked selection, Save, Cancel, and Delete.

 - Assign a physical-button-only Home/Reader shortcut that returns from nested reader menus directly to the open book, and otherwise returns Home.
 - Turn reading stats tracking on or off for the whole device or individual EPUB and XTC books, while keeping saved history and Time Left estimates.
@@ -118,6 +127,28 @@

 - OPDS and download logs hide URL tokens, fragments, and embedded credentials.

+### crASHink patch updates
+
+- Fixed: crossing pages during a drag invalidates the old page framebuffer before drawing the new selection.
+- Changed: center the floating toolbar on the selection with an 8-pixel gap, adjusting only to clear visible handles or screen edges.
+- Added: tap saved highlights for on-page edge handles and a floating pencil/trash toolbar with rounded corners, a subtle shadow and round stem handles. The toolbar uses a shared action list and wraps automatically for future options. Dragging hides the toolbar; releasing saves the resized range and returns directly to reading without reopening the toolbar while preserving text on other pages. Uncertain text mappings keep the full editor available without guessing a boundary.
+- Changed: hold briefly (200 ms) to start selection, then drag freely. Only release decides the action: one word opens the dictionary, multiple words save a highlight. Pausing while holding never opens a dictionary popup. Dictionary lookup also works on highlighted words.
+- Changed: saved clippings open directly in the full editor, with Save, Open, Delete and a top-right close button. Save is disabled when the selection matches the original, including after reversing changes.
+- Changed: selected highlights form continuous blocks across inter-word spaces on each line, without coloring outside the selected endpoints.
+- Changed: successful highlights save silently without the Clipping saved toast or its pause; save errors remain visible.
+- Performance: touch drags coalesce to the latest finger endpoint, invert only words entering or leaving the range, and avoid full-page repaints for large selections. Saved-highlight resizing also reuses the current page, restoring only two small handle regions (512 bytes). Input and release are retained during panel refresh; dragging into the broad bottom margin for 200 ms advances without having to hit the last word first. Resting on text never advances; selection hit boxes stay inside actual words and the Home swipe is suppressed during word selection.
+- Performance: cache nearby words and queue word-control clicks during e-ink refreshes instead of rescanning the chapter for every click.
+
+- Keep every clipping reachable when TOC labels overlap: group by logical chapter and saved title, refresh on store changes, and freeze each rendered row window during navigation. Failed previews remain visible as selectable entries. Merge title-spacing variants and EPUB parts belonging to the same contents entry into one chapter header.
+
+- Read saved chapter titles through one shared clipping reader when grouping the full list.
+
+- Delete in the highlight editor now acts immediately without an extra confirmation.
+
+
+- Reject partial/truncated clipping loads and block writes after load errors. Recover complete backup/temp files left by interrupted saves, and retry a transient load failure without discarding history.
+
+- Use right/down disclosure icons and indent highlight children. Tapping a clipping offers Open in book, Edit highlight and immediate Delete. The footer shows the full clipping count, current/total list pages and previous/next controls.
 ## [v1.6.0] - 2026-09-21

 ### Added
@@ -614,3 +645,9 @@
 - Power-button shortcut conflicts outside the reader so reader-only actions fall back to `Confirm` while Sleep, Refresh, Screenshot, Sync Progress, and File Transfer remain real power actions.
 - Potential crash when using `Go to %` in EPUBs.
 - Potential crash when entering sleep with Page Overlay enabled if the cached EPUB page data is invalid.
+
+### crASHink page-turn performance
+
+- Reuse one clipping-file reader per render, filter impossible highlight matches before SD reads, and collect short boundary candidates in one matching pass. Filters are session-only, conservative, and invalidated after edits.
+- Cache nearby pages' resolved highlights (including empty results) and prepare them in bounded idle slices; invalidate after clipping edits, sync/reloads, chapter or layout changes. Prepared page turns do no clipping-text reads or matching.
+- Start touch word selection after a 200 ms stationary hold instead of one second; immediate swipes remain page turns.
